#
# Conch, hearing devices and sound alerts: layer 141 of the matrix. Pair
# hearing devices, set each band's gain under a cap the owner sets, the
# balance between the ears and mono, and show sound alerts as a screen
# flash and vibration. Alerts come from the notices zxvd keeps
# (notes.list); their time from zxvd's clock (sys.info's time_ms).
#
# Advisory only: this is not a clinical fitting, and the cap is a safety
# ceiling the owner sets. Every setting (a pairing, a gain, the cap, the
# loudest input, the balance, an alert's pattern) changes only on the
# owner's confirmed word, and a gain or cap that would put a band past
# the cap is refused, never turned down silently (conch_model.h CM1-CM7).
#
# zxvd has no audio-device method: none pairs a hearing device, sets its
# gain or balance, or plays to it, and none is invented. Conch keeps the
# pairing and the settings on its own side for the view to apply, and
# changes nothing in zxvd but the notices' read marks, when the owner
# dismisses the alerts (notes.mark_read, on the owner's word).
#
#   hearing_level_ok    one band's gain (-300..300 tenths of a dB), the
#                       level it would play and the owner's cap (each
#                       0..1200 tenths of a dB SPL), the level no louder
#                       than the cap. Eve, witnessed by KRON: Eve answers
#                       only truths and holds each field against its own
#                       range, so the level under the cap, a relation
#                       across fields, is KRON's half; a level past the
#                       cap is held (BOTH), never played.
#   hearing_balance_ok  balance -100..100 and mono 0..1, Eve's ranges.
#   sound_alert_map_ok  a sound kind's flash and vibrate pulses as a
#                       ^ZXCONCH record (MYRA), witnessed by Eve: sound
#                       1..5 and 0..3 pulses each, 334 ms apart, so a
#                       screen never flashes more than three times a
#                       second. MYRA's digits hold more, so a pattern past
#                       Eve's ranges is held. The task asks for MYRA; the
#                       flash limit is a safety limit, which Eve owns, so
#                       Eve witnesses it.
#
# Kept in C, since no runnable language owns it: which sound kind a
# notice's kind text is (text matching, Raku's planned kind of work, with
# no entry of its own here), and what each ear plays of a level at a
# balance (conch_rules.h CN4, the view's mix, not a decision of what is
# allowed).
#
# Nothing nearer the core fits: the task's matrix line says this layer
# leans on no other layer's code. warble.volume_cap_ok is a volume in
# percent under a cap in percent; a hearing device's level is in tenths of
# a dB SPL with a per-band gain range beside it, another rule.
#
# Planned languages: LabVIEW (dataflow, signal) for a band's output level;
# Gleam (messaging, types) for the alert a notice becomes; Raku (parse,
# text) has no entry here (the notice kind's text is matched in C).
zxapp 1
id     conch
name   Conch
version 1.0.0
slot   141
layer  L1
matrix 141
icon   icons/l1/141-conch.svg
budget 233
needs  notify
needs  sys.read
model  apps/conch_model.c

# One band's level under the owner's cap (CN1): Eve, witnessed by KRON.
provides hearing_level_ok truth gain total cap
logic    eve  hearing_level_ok apps/blocks/conch/level.eve
logic    kron hearing_level_ok apps/blocks/conch/level.kron
pending  LabVIEW hearing_level_ok

# The balance between the ears and mono (CN2): Eve.
provides hearing_balance_ok truth balance mono
logic    eve hearing_balance_ok apps/blocks/conch/balance.eve

# A sound kind's flash and vibrate pattern (CN3): MYRA, witnessed by Eve.
provides sound_alert_map_ok truth sound flash vibrate
logic    myra sound_alert_map_ok apps/blocks/conch/alert.myra
logic    eve  sound_alert_map_ok apps/blocks/conch/alert.eve
pending  Gleam sound_alert_map_ok

# Its own proof (zxapp.h K1): each entry at its edges, and where its languages disagree
check hearing_level_ok gain=0,300,301,-300,-301,250,100 total=650,950,951,350,349,900,1201 cap=900,950,1000,900,900,900,1201 = true,true,false,true,false,true,false
check hearing_level_ok gain=0,0,0 total=-1,0,1200 cap=0,-1,1200 = false,false,true
check hearing_level_ok gain=0,100 total=650,951 cap=900,950 = both
check hearing_balance_ok balance=-100,0,100,-101,101,0,0 mono=0,1,1,0,0,2,-1 = true,true,true,false,false,false,false
check sound_alert_map_ok sound=1,5,3,10,1,1 flash=0,3,3,0,10,0 vibrate=0,3,0,0,0,-10 = true,true,true,false,false,false
check sound_alert_map_ok sound=1,1 flash=1,4 vibrate=1,1 = both
check sound_alert_map_ok sound=2,0 flash=1,1 vibrate=1,1 = both
